      "shield": true,
      "title": "How do you talk about school?",
      "body": "Let's find out.",
      "notes": "Greet students. Ask: What do you like about your school? What subjects do you study?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "importance",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "title": "Why is this lesson important?",
      "body": "<ul><li>School words help you talk about your daily life.</li><li>You use them with teachers, parents, and friends.</li><li>They help you understand conversations about school.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "entry-ticket-task",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#c0392b",
      "title": "Entry Ticket &mdash; Vocabulary Test",
      "body": "<p style=\"font-size:38px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 12px 0\">Complete the test on your paper.</p><p style=\"font-size:38px;color:#fff;margin:0\">Answer all 20 questions. You have 5 minutes.</p>",
      "notes": "Students complete the 20-question Vocabulary Levels Test handout. Timer pill: 5 minutes (300 seconds)."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "entry-ticket-answers-1",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "body": "<style>.et{border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px auto;max-width:760px;width:100%}.et td{padding:7px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);color:#fff;text-align:left;font-size:34px;vertical-align:top}.et .num{color:#ffdd00;font-weight:700;min-width:30px}.et .ltr{color:#2ecc71;font-weight:900;min-width:34px}</style><h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:47px;margin-bottom:8px\">Entry Ticket &mdash; Answers</h2><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:36px;margin-bottom:8px\"><span class=\"box-word\">Swap</span> and <span class=\"box-word\">mark</span>.</p><table class=\"et\"><tr><td class=\"num\">1</td><td class=\"ltr\">D</td><td>single movement</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">2</td><td class=\"ltr\">B</td><td>being unwell</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">3</td><td class=\"ltr\">A</td><td>tall narrow building</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">4</td><td class=\"ltr\">A</td><td>higher land</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">5</td><td class=\"ltr\">B</td><td>travel by air</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">6</td><td class=\"ltr\">C</td><td>moved her hand</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">7</td><td class=\"ltr\">A</td><td>value</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">8</td><td class=\"ltr\">C</td><td>eyesight</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">9</td><td class=\"ltr\">C</td><td>not able</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">10</td><td class=\"ltr\">C</td><td>unhappy</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Answers 1-10. Students swap and mark."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "entry-ticket-answers-2",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "body": "<style>.et{border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px auto;max-width:760px;width:100%}.et td{padding:7px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);color:#fff;text-align:left;font-size:34px;vertical-align:top}.et .num{color:#ffdd00;font-weight:700;min-width:30px}.et .ltr{color:#2ecc71;font-weight:900;min-width:34px}</style><h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:47px;margin-bottom:8px\">Entry Ticket &mdash; Answers</h2><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:36px;margin-bottom:8px\"><span class=\"box-word\">Continue</span> marking.</p><table class=\"et\"><tr><td class=\"num\">11</td><td class=\"ltr\">D</td><td>helpful</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">12</td><td class=\"ltr\">B</td><td>flat</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">13</td><td class=\"ltr\">B</td><td>nice</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">14</td><td class=\"ltr\">D</td><td>written words</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">15</td><td class=\"ltr\">C</td><td>non-stop</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">16</td><td class=\"ltr\">D</td><td>sends out</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">17</td><td class=\"ltr\">A</td><td>soothed</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">18</td><td class=\"ltr\">A</td><td>order</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">19</td><td class=\"ltr\">D</td><td>music writer</td></tr><tr><td class=\"num\">20</td><td class=\"ltr\">B</td><td>very thorough</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Answers 11-20. Continue marking."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "recall-schools",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "title": "Think about school",
      "body": "<p style=\"font-size:38px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 12px 0\">Think about your school.</p><p style=\"font-size:38px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 22px 0\">What makes a good school? Talk to your partner.</p><p style=\"color:#ffdd00;text-align:center;font-size:38px;font-weight:700;margin-top:22px\">Opinion &mdash; Reason &mdash; Evidence</p>",
      "notes": "Pairs discuss for 2 minutes. Use Opinion-Reason-Evidence structure. Elicit a few ideas: good teachers, fair rules, fun activities."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "transition-vocab",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#c0392b",
      "title": "Let's check your word knowledge",
      "notes": "Transition to vocabulary presentation. Say: These are words about school. We will learn ten of them."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-allow",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/əˈlaʊ/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">allow</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Our school allows us to wear casual clothes on Fridays. The teachers say it is OK.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: If the teacher allows phones, can you use them?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-assessment",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/əˈsesmənt/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">assessment</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Her grade came from continuous assessment. The teacher watched her work all year.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Is an assessment a test of your work?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-assignments",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/əˈsaɪnmənts/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">assignments</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Our assignments are due on Friday. We must hand them to the teacher.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: What do you do with an assignment?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-ban",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/bæn/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">ban</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Our school banned food in the library. Now nobody can eat there.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: If the school bans phones, can you use them?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-behavior",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/bɪˈheɪvjə/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">behavior</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">His behavior in class is very good. He listens and works quietly.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Is talking during a lesson good behavior?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-bullying",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/ˈbʊliɪŋ/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">bullying</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Nobody should face bullying at school. Every student deserves to feel safe.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Is bullying kind or unkind behavior?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-required",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/rɪˈkwaɪəd/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">required</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Science is a required subject here. Every student must study it.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Is a required subject optional?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-educate",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/ˈedʒukeɪt/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">educate</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">Some parents educate their children at home. They teach them outside school.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Who educates you at school?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-grades",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/ɡreɪdz/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">grades</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">She got good grades in math last year. Her teacher was very happy.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Are good grades a sign of good work?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-work-experience",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;text-align:left;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:30px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0;font-size:47px\">/wɜːk ɪkˈspɪəriəns/</td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\"><span class=\"box-word\">work experience</span></td></tr><tr class=\"fragment\"><td style=\"padding:12px 0\">My sister did work experience at a hospital. She helped the nurses for a month.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Click 1: show word. Click 2: show context. CCQ: Where do you do work experience? A school or a job?"
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "transition-listen",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#c0392b",
      "title": "School Open Evening",
      "notes": "Transition to listening. Say: We will listen to a parent and a teacher talking at a school open evening."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "strategy-predict",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "title": "Strategy: Predict",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #555;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Do</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #555\">Predict what the parent will ask.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #555;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Why</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #555\">It helps your brain focus.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">How</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0\">Read the title. Think of topics.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Say: The title is School Open Evening. A parent visits. What might he ask about? Predict first, then listen."
    },
    {
      "layout": "auto-animate-pair",
      "id": "demo-predict",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#116466",
      "title": "Try it: Predict",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">A student tells a friend about her new school.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"padding:8px 0;color:#ffdd00;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Which topics might she mention?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Her favorite food.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">The school uniform.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Her new teachers.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">A movie she watched.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Ask students to predict which topics a student might mention. Click to reveal the checkmarks."
    },
    {
      "layout": "auto-animate-pair",
      "id": "demo-predict",
      "step": 2,
      "background_color": "#116466",
      "title": "Try it: Predict",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">A student tells a friend about her new school.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"padding:8px 0;color:#ffdd00;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Which topics might she mention?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Her favorite food.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center;color:#2ecc71;font-weight:900\">✓</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">The school uniform.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center;color:#2ecc71;font-weight:900\">✓</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Her new teachers.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;width:36px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;border-bottom:1px solid #444\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:24px;text-align:center\">&nbsp;</span></td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">A movie she watched.</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Revealed: uniform and teachers make sense. Food and movies are less likely for a school talk."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "gist-task",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:48px;margin-bottom:20px\">Listen &mdash; Gist</h2><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:38px;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto\">What is Mr. Harris choosing?</p><div style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:24px\"><audio controls data-src=\"assets/dialog.mp3\" style=\"width:340px\"></audio></div>",
      "notes": "Play the dialog once. Students listen for the gist only: What is the parent choosing? Answer: a school for his son."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "gist-answer",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "title": "Gist — Answer",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top;width:90px\">Question</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">What is Mr. Harris choosing?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Answer</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">He is choosing a school for his son.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Explanation</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">He asks about classes, grades, phones, and bullying.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Transcript</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0\">“We're choosing a school for my son.”</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Confirm the gist. The parent wants to find the right school for his son."
    },
    {
      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "detail-task",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:48px;margin-bottom:20px\">Listen again</h2><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:36px;margin-bottom:16px\">Answer the questions.</p><div style=\"max-width:820px;margin:0 auto\"><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:34px;margin:10px 0\">1. How does the school teach students?</p><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:34px;margin:10px 0\">2. How does a student get a grade?</p><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:34px;margin:10px 0\">3. When can students use phones?</p><p style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:34px;margin:10px 0\">4. What happens in the final year?</p></div><div style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:16px\"><audio controls data-src=\"assets/dialog.mp3\" style=\"width:340px\"></audio></div>",
      "notes": "Play the dialog again. Students answer the four detail questions. Then go through the answer slides."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "answer-d1",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "title": "Answers (1/4)",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top;width:90px\">Question</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">1. How does the school teach students?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Answer</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">With small classes and plenty of discussion.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Explanation</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Ms. Clark describes the teaching method first.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Transcript</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0\">“We use small classes and plenty of discussion.”</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Check the answer. Elicit: small classes and discussion."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "answer-d2",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "title": "Answers (2/4)",
      "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top;width:90px\">Question</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">2. How does a student get a grade?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Answer</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Through continuous assessment, from work all year.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Explanation</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #444\">Grades come from assignments written every month, not one exam.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px 8px 0;font-weight:700;color:#ffdd00;white-space:nowrap;vertical-align:top\">Transcript</td><td style=\"padding:8px 0\">“We use continuous assessment. A student's grade comes from their work all year.”</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "Check the answer. Point out the word assessment from the vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "layout": "content",
      "id": "answer-d3",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#052e0d",
      "title": "Answers (3/4)",
